  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Study visit on Sustainable Energy and PPPs for Lebanese energy stakeholders</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This activity involved the organisation and coordination of a four day study visit to the Netherlands (2-5 February 2026) for a Lebanese delegation of 12 representatives from the Berytech SE Cluster, the Lebanese Center for Energy Conservation and the Ministry of Energy and Water. The visit included programme development, participant coordination, logistics and on site support.The programme provided insights into Dutch approaches to public private partnerships for sustainable energy, including financing and risk mitigation mechanisms. It also introduced participants to practices in renewable energy integration, such as smart metering, storage and solar solutions.The visit further aimed to strengthen institutional and business ties between Lebanese and Dutch stakeholders and explore opportunities for future cooperation.</narrative>
  </description>
